---
import ChevronDown from '@lucide/astro/icons/chevron-down';

const faqs = [
  {
    question: 'Why Not Just Use VS Code, Cursor, Or Another AI IDE?',
    answer: 'Most AI IDEs wrap one chat backend inside an Electron shell and tie you to one provider. Alera is terminal-first: it runs any CLI agent, several at once, each in its own worktree, in a native app with no Electron and no bundled Chromium.',
  },
  {
    question: 'How Do I Bring My Own Agent?',
    answer: 'If it runs in a terminal, it runs in Alera. Open a terminal tab in a workspace and launch the CLI like you would in any shell. Claude Code, Codex, Amp, Antigravity, OpenCode, Cursor, Copilot, Pi, Grok Build, and fx also report live states once you turn on their status hooks in Settings.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Do I Need Git To Use Alera?',
    answer: 'No. A plain folder gets a single workspace with terminals and agents. Git-backed projects unlock the worktree workflow, where each task gets its own checkout and branch.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Can Agents Run On Another Machine?',
    answer: 'Yes. Add a machine under Settings, Remote Hosts, and Alera installs its runtime there over SSH. Workspaces on that host run their terminals, files, and Git where the code lives, and show up in the same sidebar.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Is There A Mobile App?',
    answer: 'The Android companion pairs with your runtime to show agent states, send a push when an agent needs you, and open its terminal so you can answer. It is published as an APK on GitHub Releases; an iOS release is planned.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Do I Need An Account?',
    answer: 'No. Everything local works without one. An optional Alera account adds mobile push and the encrypted relay for reaching your runtime from outside your network. Pushes never carry prompts, commands, terminal output, or source code, and the relay only forwards end-to-end encrypted traffic it cannot read.',
  },
];
---

<section id="faq" class="defer-offscreen-rendering border-t border-border-subtle/50 px-6 py-24">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
    <div class="mb-14 text-center">
      <p class="mb-4 font-mono text-label-md uppercase tracking-widest text-foreground-faint">FAQ</p>
      <h2 class="mb-4 text-headline-lg font-semibold tracking-tight text-foreground md:text-[32px]">Questions, Answered</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-3">
      {
        faqs.map((faq) => (
          <details class="group rounded-xl border border-border bg-surface transition-colors duration-mid hover:border-foreground-faint/20">
            <summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 px-5 py-4 text-body-md font-medium text-foreground [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
              <span>{faq.question}</span>
              <ChevronDown size={16} class="shrink-0 text-foreground-faint transition-transform duration-fast group-open:rotate-180" />
            </summary>
            <div class="-mt-1 px-5 pb-5">
              <p class="text-body-md leading-relaxed text-foreground-muted">{faq.answer}</p>
            </div>
          </details>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
